# ripgrep default-search exclusions for immutable or historical bulk.
# No gate reads this file. Include everything with: rg --no-ignore-dot
#
# Precisely: no gate's result depends on it. The Python gates use os.walk and
# open(), `git grep` ignores it, and cargo-mutants copies the tree with .ignore
# disabled. The one gate tool that honours it is `cargo machete`
# (scripts/quality.sh), and only to find Cargo.toml manifests, so never list a
# directory that holds a Cargo.toml.
#
# Rules for entries: only bulk that nobody edits and that dominates search
# hits. Ledgers an agent edits stay visible (docs/quality/owners.json,
# exception-growth.json, source-allowances.json, policy.json, everything in
# docs/refactor/, verification/manifest.json, verification/receipts/).
# Hidden files stay readable by path; docs/README.md says what each holds.
# Search the root or one directory at a time. With several path arguments
# (rg X src docs), ripgrep 15.1.0 applies this file only intermittently; that
# fails open, showing the hidden files.
# Measured when added, over 7 core identifiers: 2,192 -> 1,090 hit lines,
# 412 -> 305 files.

# Adoption diagnostics, sha256-pinned in docs/quality/policy.json (1.7 MB).
/docs/quality/legacy-diagnostics.json
/docs/quality/legacy-diagnostics-linux.json

# September 2026 hardening program: per-round implementation plans (4 MB),
# raw evidence and the end-of-batch report. The directory's live files
# (README.md, NEXT-WORK.md, edge-changes.md, effective-config-diff.md) stay
# visible.
/docs/reviews/2026-09-hardening/plans/
/docs/reviews/2026-09-hardening/evidence/
/docs/reviews/2026-09-hardening/report/

# A July 2026 performance diff.
/docs/reviews/*.patch

# Published read-experiment measurements (3.8 MB), checked by
# scripts/read-experiments/followup/verify_published.py.
/docs/read-experiments/followup/*.json

# The WP-00 restructuring work package, written against 685ea035 (192 KB).
/codereview1.md

# The August 2026 multitenancy conversion map (190 KB). Its line anchors decay
# by design; scripts/multitenancy-audit.sh is the enforcement now.
/docs/MULTITENANCY-MAP.md
